# SHA-256 of the LALPulsar ephemeris tables gwmock-signal reads: the solar-system delays of every
# projection, on by default, and the continuous-wave barycentring.
#
# These are physics inputs, not build artefacts: they define the Earth and Sun trajectories, so a
# change to their content changes generated strain. gwmock-signal fetches them by name from the
# LALSuite repository into its cache, and refuses a table under such a name whose SHA-256 is not the
# one it records (`RECORDED_SHA256` in `gwmock_signal.projection.solar_system`). The lines below are
# those values, and must stay equal to them.
#
# CI derives its ephemeris cache identifier from this file, so editing it invalidates the cache.
# Only the compressed tables are listed because they are the ones read by name; gwmock-signal also
# records the uncompressed `.dat` digests.
#
# If gwmock-signal refuses a table: either the cache is corrupt (clear it and refetch) or upstream
# changed the tables. The second case is worth understanding before updating these lines, because it
# means the reference trajectories moved.
#
# **Updating these hashes changes generated strain, so regenerate the e2e references in the same
# commit** -- every signal reference under `tests/e2e/references/` was produced against the tables
# below. Nothing enforces that pairing: split across two commits, the reference comparison fails on
# the second one and looks like a code regression.
4995647b2c47617c90804ad0bc814ce42b426f1e5015a90cf939bcdd0c20ea67  earth00-40-DE405.dat.gz
0b132dc5a712ebc16661a10cb88409e2577c16723c64f98e9b9b4d265510700f  sun00-40-DE405.dat.gz
